{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113697","id":3078644528,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc63gGMw","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113697","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113697.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113697.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113697","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113697/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113697/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113697/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/b15f9deffbf1ef54a867ea0786b4f86e1fa03fa9","number":113697,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Use structured data for \"deprecated\" in `gdextension_interface.json`","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"In [updating godot-cpp](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-cpp/pull/1895) to use the [new `gdextension_interface.json` file](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107845), I ended up needing to know which Godot version each interface function was deprecated in, so that I could properly implement a `deprecated=no` option.\r\n\r\nThis information is in the deprecated message for all interface functions currently, but the presence of this text isn't enforced.\r\n\r\nThis PR makes \"deprecated\" into structured data that looks like:\r\n\r\n```js\r\n{\r\n  // ...\r\n  \"deprecated\": {\r\n    \"since\": \"4.6\",\r\n    \"message\": \"Does not allow explicitly requesting padding.\",\r\n    \"replace_with\": \"mem_alloc2\"\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI ended up only making \"since\" required, because retroactively writing all the \"message\"s would be onerous. Later, if we want, we can fill them in and make it required.\r\n\r\nAlso, the Python code validates that the replacement actually exists and that it isn't deprecated too, which should help to prevent errors. It even found one error right away, which I think already justifies switching to structured data. :-)\r\n\r\n_(Note: I'm targeting this for Godot 4.6 because it's a tweak to a new feature added in Godot 4.6.)_\r\n\r\n### Original Description\r\n\r\nThis PR puts a pattern on the JSON schema that enforces that this text will always be there! This way the regex I added in godot-cpp can't be broken in the future.\r\n\r\nHowever, this makes me wonder if this shouldn't be structured data instead? I'm not sure how that should look, though? It could maybe be:\r\n\r\n```\r\n{\r\n  // ...\r\n  \"deprecated\": {\r\n    \"since\": \"4.5\",\r\n    \"message\": \"Use mem_alloc2 instead.\"\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThat begs the question of if the replacement (ex `mem_alloc2` in this case) shouldn't be in structured data too? But I'm very unsure about that, because a replacement isn't required: a function can be deprecated and replaced with nothing, or there could even be multiple replacements depending on context. That's why this is a free-form text field to begin with.\r\n\r\nSo, this PR takes the easy path, and just mandates that it must start with the pattern that includes the deprecated version. And maybe that's OK?","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":580537003,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1ODA1MzcwMDM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdextension","name":"topic:gdextension","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12939969,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AxXLB","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/23","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23/labels","number":23,"state":"closed","title":"4.6","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issu